cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If Aegis QEC contributes to your research, please cite this software and the decoder papers used by your experiment."
title: "Aegis QEC"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bahri"
    given-names: "Hamid"
version: 1.1.1
date-released: 2026-10-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hamidbahri92/Aegis"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/aegis-qec/"
abstract: "An open-source Python toolkit for quantum error correction and surface-code decoding using PyMatching sparse-blossom MWPM, explicit Stim detector-error-model inputs, calibrated decoding experiments, correction-edge reconstruction, and reproducible validation and benchmarking workflows."
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - QEC
  - surface code
  - rotated surface code
  - quantum decoding
  - minimum-weight perfect matching
  - sparse blossom
  - PyMatching
  - Stim
  - detector error model
  - fault-tolerant quantum computing
